WEBVTT

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:18.640
Do you hear?  Hooves beating

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:30.750
A carriage goes through the gentle hills

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:38.030
Someone comes to pick me up

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:45.980
And takes me

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:49.950
To the avenue with white flowers

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:58.070
To the home of wind

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.450
He takes me

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.900
I'm sure

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:48.250
The weather is fine so this year
we may have a good harvest.

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:49.770
Well now, yes.

00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:59.040
Rachel said that they have already
started harvesting the oats yesterday.

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:03.790
Well now, is that child still asleep?

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:07.060
It's still too early for school.

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:10.650
Well yes, too early for school.

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:14.150
I hope she can concentrate on the lessons.

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:18.080
Well now, don't be too worried.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:25.080
Nothing should go wrong if she's with Diana,

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:27.170
but her character is too weird.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:32.130
Speaking of school, we don't
even know what's going on there.

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:36.420
Well now... don't be to worried about that.

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:44.270
If only was that easy.

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:53.470
I'm leaving.

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:07.600
I´m starting school today.

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:14.420
Matthew, good morning!

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:15.850
I'm going to school today!

00:03:16.470 --> 00:03:19.040
Well now. Work hard.

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:20.470
Don't worry!

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:22.180
Have a nice trip.

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:23.650
Yes.

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:32.630
What a splendid day!

00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:37.790
Diana, good morning!

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:53.700
Good morning, Marilla.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.760
Why are you up so early?

00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:58.480
Because there's school today.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:02.270
I woke up when Matthew
and Jerry were leaving.

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:05.560
We're going to harvest from now on,
so they'll be up especially early.

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:07.750
You could have slept a while more.

00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:08.670
I'm alright.

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:10.520
Let me help you.

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:13.240
Alright.
I'll leave this to you then.

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:15.600
I'll go milk the cows.

00:04:57.160 --> 00:04:58.220
It's all done.

00:04:58.660 --> 00:05:02.320
If only you were like this everyday,
I wouldn't be having such a hard life.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:05.380
I want to be like this everyday too.

00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:07.600
Is that my lunch?

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:08.900
Yes, it is.

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:13.700
How wonderful. I can take
a lunch basket to school.

00:05:14.050 --> 00:05:18.090
Although I did it before at Mrs. Thomas,

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:20.410
but it was hard bread every time.

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:22.180
I wonder what's inside?

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:26.740
I hardly see you up so early,
so don't waste time and eat your breakfast.

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:31.550
Even if you have school,
the dishes are still your duty.

00:05:31.550 --> 00:05:32.980
Yes, I know.

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:35.420
Anne!

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:37.360
Yes...

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:55.190
I will be meeting Diana
on the bridge on Lover's Lane.

00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:57.590
Lover's Lane?

00:05:57.850 --> 00:05:59.630
The lane behind the field.

00:05:59.870 --> 00:06:02.730
Not that lovers ever really walk there,

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:07.510
but Diana and I are reading a magnificent
book and there's a Lover's Lane in it.

00:06:07.510 --> 00:06:10.850
So we want to have one, too.

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:13.040
And it's a very pretty name, don't you think?

00:06:13.340 --> 00:06:15.100
So romantic!

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:19.220
We can't imagine the lovers into it,
you know.

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:21.450
I like Lover's Lane.

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:28.720
Because you can think out loud there
without people calling you crazy.

00:06:30.420 --> 00:06:33.980
Anne, don't talk like that
when you are having classes.

00:06:33.980 --> 00:06:35.050
Don't worry.

00:06:35.050 --> 00:06:37.960
Now hurry up, Diana will be
waiting if you don't go out now.

00:06:38.310 --> 00:06:39.430
It's already so late?

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:42.740
Then, I'm going!

00:06:42.740 --> 00:06:46.260
And don't throw a tantrum,
no matter what happens.

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:47.560
I'll be alright.

00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:53.100
I'm going, Snow Queen!

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:56.330
Be careful not to fall!

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:57.480
Don't worry!

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:28.050
Anne Shirley of Green Gables!

00:08:28.050 --> 00:08:29.050
Diana!

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:32.060
You're early, Anne? Have you waited long?

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:35.320
No I didn't Diana, I just arrived.

00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:36.540
This way, right?

00:08:36.940 --> 00:08:37.940
That's right!

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:54.170
Anne, could we rest for a while?

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:56.800
We won't be late!

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:57.800
But...

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:00.240
We are not late, Anne!

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:02.040
Right...

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:04.230
That's true.

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:05.230
Yes, it is.

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:08.480
You seem very nervous.

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:09.480
It's not that.

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:13.400
In the asylum I used to run all the time.

00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:17.010
No wonder I couldn't catch up with you.

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:20.610
But what a splendid day!

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:23.690
Isn't it good just to be alive on a day like this?

00:09:24.230 --> 00:09:28.200
I pity the people who aren't born
yet for missing it.

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:32.340
They may have good days, of course,

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:35.760
but they can never have this one.

00:09:36.100 --> 00:09:41.410
And it's splendider still to have such
a lovely way to go to school by,

00:09:41.410 --> 00:09:42.070
isn't it?

00:09:42.070 --> 00:09:47.690
It's a lot nicer than going around by
the road, that is so dusty and hot.

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:48.880
Look over there.

00:09:52.530 --> 00:09:56.450
There are a lot of violets amongst
those withered trees during spring.

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:57.800
Really so much?

00:09:57.870 --> 00:09:59.890
So many you wouldn't have a place to stand.

00:10:18.850 --> 00:10:20.050
Diana.

00:10:20.360 --> 00:10:26.110
Then, Diana, why don't we
call that place Violet Vale?

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:27.960
Violet Vale?

00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:29.650
That's right.

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:34.500
Although it has no violets now,
we can imagine it has a lot of them.

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:37.060
That's true. It´s wonderful.

00:10:37.460 --> 00:10:39.500
But this isn't a valley.

00:10:40.060 --> 00:10:42.440
But isn't better to have a beautiful name?

00:10:42.440 --> 00:10:45.150
And we can imagine that it is a valley.

00:10:46.090 --> 00:10:47.130
Well, that's right.

00:10:53.050 --> 00:10:57.260
After this we'll get back to the
main road, and reach school soon.

00:10:57.260 --> 00:10:59.350
What a beautiful road filled with birches.

00:10:59.350 --> 00:11:02.120
Wait, let me try to change
the name of this place.

00:11:02.600 --> 00:11:04.310
All right, Diana.

00:11:04.900 --> 00:11:07.200
Well... then...

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:09.400
Why not call it Birch Path?

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:10.520
Yes...

00:11:23.260 --> 00:11:24.200
It's over there.

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:36.700
That's school.

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:38.300
That's right.

00:11:58.570 --> 00:11:59.310
Over here!

00:12:00.870 --> 00:12:01.720
Welcome!

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:12.160
Good morning!

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:15.660
I always put the milk here to cool till noon.

00:12:15.660 --> 00:12:17.470
You can put yours beside mine.

00:12:17.470 --> 00:12:18.770
It's really a good idea.

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:23.600
Good morning!

00:12:23.860 --> 00:12:24.960
Good morning, Tillie.

00:12:25.540 --> 00:12:26.830
Good morning, Anne.

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:29.960
Good morning... Tillie.

00:12:47.390 --> 00:12:49.000
Good morning!

00:13:04.070 --> 00:13:05.370
Good morning, Diana.

00:13:05.790 --> 00:13:06.750
Good morning, Ruby.

00:13:12.160 --> 00:13:13.660
My seat is here.

00:13:14.470 --> 00:13:16.630
You can sit beside me.

00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:21.930
This seat has been always empty,
so I think teacher Phillips wont mind.

00:13:22.090 --> 00:13:24.280
It's wonderful that I can sit beside you.

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:27.000
Is the teacher someone scary?

00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:28.730
Yes... But...

00:13:32.140 --> 00:13:33.530
The teacher is coming!

00:13:34.180 --> 00:13:36.860
Good morning.

00:13:37.300 --> 00:13:39.210
Prissy is grown up,

00:13:39.470 --> 00:13:41.760
and the teacher is dead gone on her.

00:13:49.630 --> 00:13:52.020
Good morning, everyone.

00:13:52.020 --> 00:13:54.210
Good morning!

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:00.650
Then...

00:14:02.880 --> 00:14:04.430
Anne Shirley.

00:14:05.470 --> 00:14:09.140
You must be Anne Shirley
from the orphan asylum?

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:11.070
That's right.

00:14:11.300 --> 00:14:13.910
But I came from Green Gables!

00:14:20.550 --> 00:14:24.080
With eleven years old,
you should be in the fifth grade,

00:14:24.080 --> 00:14:26.930
but until where did you study at the asylum?

00:14:27.160 --> 00:14:29.300
The middle of the fourth book.

00:14:29.530 --> 00:14:31.210
Is that so?

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:34.680
Then you can go to fourth grade.

00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:42.060
No, it´s alright.
You can sit there for now.

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:53.200
Well... Today is the start of a new semester,
and as usual, the boys don't really turn up.

00:14:53.530 --> 00:14:57.370
Sophia Sloane, why didn't your
younger brother came to school today?

00:14:58.210 --> 00:15:00.800
Charlie had to stay to help in the work.

00:15:05.030 --> 00:15:06.860
I know that.

00:15:06.860 --> 00:15:13.810
I mean to say, I think the request
for boys to come to school

00:15:13.820 --> 00:15:16.250
has been thoroughly forgotten.

00:15:16.820 --> 00:15:19.360
Everybody's so busy, how could they come?

00:15:19.360 --> 00:15:25.040
Even if it is a busy time for agriculture,
they have to come to school.

00:15:25.250 --> 00:15:28.790
Well, we'll forget about this.
The school officially begins.

00:15:29.260 --> 00:15:30.510
look forward!

00:15:33.560 --> 00:15:37.220
Roman Campbell, you still didn't lost that
habit of not paying attention, have you?

00:15:37.500 --> 00:15:38.070
Yes...

00:15:43.150 --> 00:15:46.830
Now it's the season for peaches and pears.

00:15:46.830 --> 00:15:53.040
Hear the cries of birds from afar,
the gathering of snow on mountaintops.

00:15:53.040 --> 00:15:59.380
Life is slowly vanishing as
the mountains gather snow.

00:16:00.070 --> 00:16:03.160
What a wonderful poem.
I feel so touched.

00:16:06.800 --> 00:16:10.370
Life is slowly vanishing...

00:16:11.000 --> 00:16:15.240
as the mountains gather snow.

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:17.910
Anne!

00:16:20.980 --> 00:16:24.560
Anne Shirley, you seem
to be rather free and easy.

00:16:24.560 --> 00:16:30.230
No, well... Its because what the
teacher said was too good, so...

00:16:30.520 --> 00:16:33.990
Although there should be time for relaxation.

00:16:33.990 --> 00:16:35.770
Then let's see...

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:39.380
But... your spelling is disgraceful.

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:45.580
You seem to have read prose like this before.

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:48.430
Well, have you?

00:16:50.210 --> 00:16:52.570
Then, what about your work?

00:16:54.190 --> 00:16:57.270
This is wrong! You don't understand!

00:16:58.270 --> 00:17:00.980
Yes, because nobody taught me the right way.

00:17:01.130 --> 00:17:02.080
Anne Shirley,

00:17:02.330 --> 00:17:06.360
if this is the fruit of your
labour I can bear with it.

00:17:06.430 --> 00:17:07.360
But...

00:17:07.360 --> 00:17:08.970
Everybody look!

00:17:09.220 --> 00:17:14.130
How could you sit in for lessons like this?

00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:24.200
Anne Shirley, do this one more time!

00:17:27.310 --> 00:17:32.260
Then, Prissy, we'll practice Canada's history.

00:17:36.440 --> 00:17:38.360
Don't mind that, Anne.

00:17:38.950 --> 00:17:40.580
The teacher is always like that.

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:41.580
That's right.

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:45.000
Thank you. But I can't help it.

00:17:45.130 --> 00:17:47.290
My math has always been bad.

00:17:48.980 --> 00:17:50.040
He should be...

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:51.640
Right?

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:56.240
Quiet.

00:17:58.730 --> 00:18:02.160
When I tell you to shut up is for you to do so.

00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:32.760
But this is the first day in school for Anne.
He shouldn't be so hard on her.

00:18:32.760 --> 00:18:34.760
That's right. That was too much.

00:18:34.760 --> 00:18:35.900
This is for you to eat.

00:18:36.550 --> 00:18:38.400
I'll always be behind you.

00:18:38.490 --> 00:18:39.810
Thank you, Ruby!

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:44.450
You can wear this for the whole afternoon.

00:18:46.300 --> 00:18:48.430
It's going to protect you from teacher Phillips.

00:18:53.840 --> 00:18:55.000
Thank you, everyone.

00:18:55.230 --> 00:18:57.540
To show my gratitude,
I'm going to recite that poem.

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:07.200
Now it's the season for peaches and pears.

00:19:13.100 --> 00:19:16.250
Hear the cries of birds from afar.

00:19:28.520 --> 00:19:33.270
Life is slowly vanishing as
the mountains gather snow.

00:19:40.300 --> 00:19:41.570
Amazing!

00:19:42.250 --> 00:19:44.020
Anne, you're great!

00:19:48.450 --> 00:19:51.790
Hey, let's all sing "Nelly of Hazel Dell" together!

00:19:51.800 --> 00:19:53.160
Of course!

00:20:35.820 --> 00:20:37.020
Goodbye!

00:20:37.540 --> 00:20:39.270
See you tomorrow!

00:20:47.120 --> 00:20:47.970
I'm home!

00:20:48.950 --> 00:20:51.830
Welcome back. How was school?

00:20:51.830 --> 00:20:54.570
I think I'm going to like school here.

00:20:54.650 --> 00:20:56.600
Really? I'm relieved.

00:20:57.330 --> 00:21:00.100
I don't think much of the master, through.

00:21:00.110 --> 00:21:05.380
He's all the time curling his mustache
and making eyes at Prissy Andrews.

00:21:05.550 --> 00:21:08.270
Prissy is grown up, you know.

00:21:08.270 --> 00:21:11.770
She's sixteen and she's studying to
go to Queen's Academy next year.

00:21:11.770 --> 00:21:14.990
She sits in the long seat at the back
and he sits there, too.

00:21:14.990 --> 00:21:17.270
Most of the time to explain
her lessons, he says.

00:21:17.270 --> 00:21:21.830
But everyone says the master is
DEAD GONE on her.

00:21:21.830 --> 00:21:26.240
Ruby Gillis says she saw him
writing something on her slate

00:21:26.240 --> 00:21:30.400
and when Prissy read it she blushed
as red as a beet and giggled.

00:21:30.630 --> 00:21:32.970
And she doesn't believe it had
anything to do with the lesson.

00:21:32.970 --> 00:21:34.010
Anne Shirley!

00:21:34.440 --> 00:21:38.370
Don't let me hear you talking about
your teacher in that way again.

00:21:40.160 --> 00:21:43.910
You don't go to school to criticize the master.

00:21:43.910 --> 00:21:46.600
I guess he can teach YOU something.

00:21:46.800 --> 00:21:51.060
Understand? You are not to
come home telling tales about him.

00:21:51.060 --> 00:21:53.740
But Mr. Philips was terrible. I was...

00:21:53.740 --> 00:21:56.060
Not another word!

00:21:56.300 --> 00:21:58.530
I hope you were a good girl.

00:21:58.530 --> 00:22:02.820
Indeed I was. And everyone is friendly.

00:22:02.820 --> 00:22:05.050
I made many friends.

00:22:05.580 --> 00:22:08.030
Because of Diana we got
to know each other quickly.

00:22:08.310 --> 00:22:11.470
We all even sang
Nelly of the Hazel Dell together at lunch.

00:22:11.470 --> 00:22:14.920
I'm so glad Diana taught me that song.

00:22:14.920 --> 00:22:17.000
How were the lessons?

00:22:18.260 --> 00:22:22.400
I'm dreadfully far behind the others.

00:22:23.200 --> 00:22:27.570
Diana and the others are all in the fifth book
and I'm only in the fourth.

00:22:27.570 --> 00:22:28.770
It's kind of a disgrace.

00:22:30.200 --> 00:22:32.930
And my math was worse.

00:22:33.040 --> 00:22:36.220
But no matter what, Mr. Philips was terrible!

00:22:38.640 --> 00:22:42.540
So I decided to study hard and catch up!

00:22:43.370 --> 00:22:44.310
That's right.

00:22:44.310 --> 00:22:46.730
One must work hard to learn.

00:22:46.730 --> 00:22:48.530
And oh, Marilla,

00:22:49.270 --> 00:22:51.010
Jane Andrews told me that

00:22:51.010 --> 00:22:57.240
Minnie MacPherson told her that she
heard Prissy Andrews tell Sara Gillis

00:22:57.240 --> 00:22:59.960
that I had a very pretty nose.

00:23:00.430 --> 00:23:04.240
Marilla, that is the first compliment
I have ever had in my life

00:23:04.240 --> 00:23:06.430
and you can't imagine what
a strange feeling it gave me.

00:23:07.120 --> 00:23:09.050
Have I really a pretty nose?

00:23:09.520 --> 00:23:11.820
Marilla, I know you'll tell me the truth.

00:23:12.880 --> 00:23:15.250
Your nose is well enough.

00:23:15.250 --> 00:23:19.300
But, Anne, hurry up and change,
then help me with dinner!

00:23:19.300 --> 00:23:22.920
Matthew and the boy
will be back all hungry soon.

00:23:23.320 --> 00:23:25.050
Yes, I'll change right away.

00:23:30.500 --> 00:23:32.540
This way, there won't be any problems.

00:23:53.500 --> 00:23:56.000
I'll like school here.

00:24:18.170 --> 00:24:23.570
The lively and handsome
Gilbert Blythe is back to school.

00:24:23.780 --> 00:24:26.600
Next of Anne of Green Gables:

00:24:26.870 --> 00:24:28.400
A Tempest in the School Teapot

00:24:28.400 --> 00:24:29.400
Please watch.
